course: dictionary
lesson: 6481
title: Proper nouns and what they tell us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word that names one particular person, place or people starts with a capital letter. Navajo is one of these names. «Native peoples of North America were many nations with hundreds of languages, such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota, Haudenosaunee, Inuit and Cree.» The capital letter tells you that Navajo names one specific group of people.
explain: The same word can do different jobs. Navajo can be a noun for the people, a noun for their language, or an adjective, as in Navajo weaving. Look at the words next to it to see which job it does. Ask yourself: is it naming something, or describing something?
explain: Context clues help again. In «Navajo weaving», the word weaving is a craft, so Navajo describes which kind of weaving it is. When a sentence is about speech and language, the meaning is the language, not the people.
fact: Navajo is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: «Navajo» as a noun means a Native American people of the south-western USA, who call themselves the Diné.
fact: «Navajo» can also mean their language, which is still spoken today.
fact: As an adjective, «Navajo» means to do with the Navajo people, as in Navajo weaving.
fact: The Navajo people live in Arizona, New Mexico and Utah, and the Navajo Nation is the largest Native American reservation by land.
exercise: In «...such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota, Haudenosaunee, Inuit and Cree», why does Navajo start with a capital letter? | *It names one particular people | It starts a new sentence | It is an adjective | It is a very long word
exercise: «Navajo weaving and silver jewellery are famous.» What job does Navajo do in this sentence? | A noun for their language | *An adjective, describing the weaving | A verb meaning to make cloth | A noun for a country
exercise: The Navajo call themselves what? | *Diné | Code Talker | Cherokee | Utah
test: In the Second World War, Navajo Code Talkers used their language to send messages the enemy could not break. What were the Code Talkers doing? | Selling silver jewellery | *Sending secret messages in their language | Building roads across the desert | Painting maps for the army
test: Which state is part of the south-western USA where the Navajo live? | *Arizona | Ohio | Florida | Maine
exam: In the sentence «Navajo weaving is famous», what does Navajo tell us? | It tells us the weaving is a language | *It tells us which people the weaving belongs to | It tells us the weaving is very old | It tells us the weaving is for sale
